---
functor: 1
title: bold
---

set heading(numbering: none)

`bold` · style · a new kind of object, often a vector.

# Form

`x.bold` on a symbol, `(a + b).bold` on a group. A recipe has one base and up to three operations.

# Examples

| Recipe | Result | Glyph |
|:--|:-:|:--|
| `v.bold` | $v.bold$ | font letter |
| `A.bold` | $A.bold$ | font letter |
| `sum.bold` | $sum.bold$ | font letter |

# Four layers

| Layer | For this operation |
|:--|:--|
| Meaning | A new kind of object, often a vector. A guideline, not a rule. |
| Style | For a kind of object, prefer `object` and a `set` rule. Use the operation for fixed notation, such as `R.bb`. |
| Construction | Another alphabet for a letter: bold, double-struck, fraktur, script, upright. |
| Glyph | The font glyph when the font has one, otherwise a built glyph kept in the recipe cache. |

# Rules

- More than three operations on one base gives a warning.
- On a single letter as the first operation, it uses the bold letter of the font. On any other base, it makes the strokes thicker.

# From LaTeX

`\mathbf{A}` and `\boldsymbol{v}` become `A.bold` and `v.bold`.

# See also

